{title: Oh My Darling, Clementine}
{artist: Percy Montrose}
{key: G}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 108}
{meta: public_domain Usually credited to Percy Montrose, published 1884.}
{meta: source Sheet music "Oh My Darling Clementine", Oliver Ditson & Co., Boston, 1884.}
{meta: arrangement Original chord arrangement for Fretlight}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
In a [G]cavern, in a [G]canyon,
Excavating for a [D]mine,[D]
Dwelt a [G]miner, forty-[G]niner,
And his [D]daughter Clemen[G]tine.[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Oh my [G]darling, oh my [G]darling,
Oh my darling Clemen[D]tine,[D]
You are [G]lost and gone for[G]ever,
Dreadful [D]sorry, Clemen[G]tine.[G]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Light she [G]was, and like a [G]fairy,
And her shoes were number [D]nine,[D]
Herring [G]boxes, without [G]topses,
Sandals [D]were for Clemen[G]tine.[G]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
